## 3. Did you miss any other migration steps?

Below is a **quick sanity‑check checklist**. Tick each box; if anything is unchecked, that’s a likely source of a broken map.

| ✅ | Step | What to verify |
|----|------|----------------|
| 1️⃣ | **Package** | `npm uninstall mapbox-gl && npm install maplibre-gl` (or CDN change). |
| 2️⃣ | **Import / CSS** | `import * as maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl';` and `import 'maplibre-gl/dist/maplibre-gl.css';` (or the `<script type="module">` CDN version). |
| 3️⃣ | **Namespace** | All `mapboxgl` → `maplibregl` (including class names in CSS: `mapboxgl-ctrl` → `maplibregl-ctrl`). |
| 4️⃣ | **Access token** | Remove any `mapboxgl.accessToken = '…'`. |
| 5️⃣ | **Style URL** | Use a non‑Mapbox style (e.g. `https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty` or a self‑hosted style JSON). |
| 6️⃣ | **Sprites / Glyphs** | If you exported a Mapbox Studio style, replace `sprite` and `glyphs` URLs with ones that point to your chosen tile source (or to a public sprite set). |
| 7️⃣ | **Plugins** | Verify each Mapbox plugin you used has a MapLibre‑compatible version (or a fork). |
| 8️⃣ | **Geocoding / Directions** | Replace Mapbox REST calls with Nominatim, OSRM, OpenRouteService, MapTiler, etc. |
| 9️⃣ | **v2‑only APIs** | Replace `setFog` → `setSky`; replace free‑camera code with `calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation` + `jumpTo/easeTo/flyTo`. |
| 🔟 | **CSS class overrides** | If you wrote custom CSS targeting `.mapboxgl-…`, rename to `.maplibregl-…`. |
| 1️⃣1️⃣ | **Test** | Open the page, check the console for “Unrecognized style property” or “Unknown source type” errors – those usually mean the style still references `mapbox://` sources. |
| 1️⃣2️⃣ | **Version** | Ensure you are using a **MapLibre v6** (or later) bundle; older v5 bundles still expose a default export (`import maplibregl from 'maplibre-gl'`) but the API surface is slightly different. |

If all of the above are satisfied **except** the two rows about `setFog` and free‑camera, you are exactly where the migration guide expects you to be.

---

## 4. What you gain / what you lose

| ✅ Gains by moving to MapLibre | ❌ What you give up |
|-------------------------------|--------------------|
| BSD‑3‑Clause open‑source license – no vendor lock‑in | Direct use of Mapbox‑hosted vector tiles (`mapbox://`) |
| No mandatory access‑token (you can still use tokens for third‑party services you choose) | Mapbox Studio style editor (you must edit styles manually or with Maputnik) |
| Ability to self‑host tiles, sprites, glyphs, or use any public source (OpenStreetMap, OpenFreeMap, PMTiles, etc.) | Built‑in Mapbox Search, Directions, Geocoding, and other SaaS APIs |
| Community‑driven roadmap, transparent releases | Official Mapbox support / SLA |
| New features first in MapLibre (e.g., globe view, adaptive composite projection, MLT tile format) | Some Mapbox‑only UI widgets that never got ported (e.g., `MapboxGeocoder` – you need a fork or a different geocoder) |

---

## 5. Next‑step code snippet (full minimal example)

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
  <meta charset="utf-8" />
  <title>MapLibre migration demo</title>
  <link href="https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.css" rel="stylesheet" />
  <style>
    #map { position:absolute; top:0; bottom:0; width:100%; }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
<div id="map"></div>

<script type="module">
  import * as maplibregl from 'https://unpkg.com/maplibre-gl@^6.0.0/dist/maplibre-gl.mjs';

  const map = new maplibregl.Map({
    container: 'map',
    style: 'https://tiles.openfreemap.org/styles/liberty', // non‑Mapbox style
    center: [-122.42, 37.78],
    zoom: 12,
    pitch: 45,
    bearing: 30
  });

  // Add navigation controls (same API)
  map.addControl(new maplibregl.NavigationControl());

  // Add sky (replaces fog)
  map.on('load', () => {
    map.setSky({
      'sky-color': '#cceeff',
      'horizon-color': '#88ccee',
      'fog-color': 'white',
      'fog-ground-blend': 0.5,
      'horizon-fog-blend': 0.3,
      'sky-horizon-blend': 0.5,
      'atmosphere-blend': 1.0
    });
  });

  // Example of moving the camera to a 3‑D position
  function goTo3D(lng, lat, altitude, bearing, pitch, roll = 0) {
    const cam = map.calculateCameraOptionsFromCameraLngLatAltRotation(
      [lng, lat],
      altitude,
      bearing,
      pitch,
      roll
    );
    map.easeTo(cam);
  }

  // Move 500 m above the map after 2 seconds
  setTimeout(() => {
    goTo3D(-122.42, 37.78, 500, 30, 45);
  }, 2000);
</script>
</body>
</html>
```

Run the snippet in a modern browser (or copy it into a local `index.html`). You should see:

* The OpenFreeMap “liberty” style.
* A sky/fog effect that mimics what

