## 1️⃣ Official Mapbox GL Geocoder (the “plug‑and‑play” way)

```html
<!-- HTML -->
<link
  href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.css"
  rel="stylesheet"
/>
<link
  href="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.css"
  rel="stylesheet"
/>
<script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/v2.15.0/mapbox-gl.js"></script>
<script src="https://api.mapbox.com/mapbox-gl-js/plugins/mapbox-gl-geocoder/v4.7.2/mapbox-gl-geocoder.min.js"></script>
```

```js
// JS
mapboxgl.accessToken = 'YOUR_MAPBOX_ACCESS_TOKEN';

const map = new mapboxgl.Map({
  container: 'map',
  style: 'mapbox://styles/mapbox/streets-v12',
  center: [-122.42, 37.78],
  zoom: 12
});

const geocoder = new MapboxGeocoder({
  accessToken: mapboxgl.accessToken,
  mapboxgl: mapboxgl,          // required for the built‑in fly‑to
  placeholder: 'Search places',
  marker: false,               // we’ll add our own marker if we want
  proximity: {
    longitude: -122.42,
    latitude: 37.78
  }
});

map.addControl(geocoder); // adds the UI to the top‑left by default
```

**Key points**

* The UI is a ready‑made `<input>` with autocomplete, keyboard navigation, and a built‑in “fly‑to” when a result is selected.
* You can customize:
  * `countries`, `types`, `language`, `bbox`, `proximity`, `limit`, etc.
  * `marker` (true/false/custom) – if you want a marker at the result.
  * `flyTo` (true/false/custom options) – you can replace the default animation with your own.
* **Pricing** – Mapbox Geocoding is billed per request (free tier 100 k/mo). Check the current pricing page.

